            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0657" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2888: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-24T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 24—2:31
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>196. Department’s telegram no. 179, July 15, 8 p.m.<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d545-f1"/> After conferring with my British colleague I venture to
                    bring to the Department’s attention the difficulties attendant upon negotiations
                    in Peking in jointly communicating the documents mentioned to the Chinese
                    Government. The matter would have to be referred by my colleagues to their
                    respective Governments and it is evident that the Japanese <pb facs="0658"
                        n="560" xml:id="pg560"/> Legation desires to delay as far as possible any
                    joint communication giving accurate information regarding consortium to the
                    Chinese Government. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
